! TDDFT mode matrix 06/16 -- global hybrid, full RPA, BOTH multiplicities
!                              + the XC-kernel self-tests
!
! The densest single case in the matrix: singlet and triplet blocks are
! assembled and diagonalized in the same run, and %tddft_selftest
! cross-checks the assembled (A+B) column against an independent
! CPKS-style build (~1e-14) and the kernel routes against finite
! differences of V_xc.
!
! This duplicates tests/test_v087_h2o_tddft.inp on purpose: that file
! is the NUMERICAL anchor (its header carries hand-verified eV values),
! this one is the MODE-COVERAGE entry.  Keep both.
!
! Physics check: every triplet must lie below its singlet partner.
%method  B3LYP
%basis   sto-3g
%job     energy
%charge  0
%mult    1
%tddft   3
%tddft_multiplicity both
%tddft_selftest on
%geom angstrom
O    0.000000    0.000000    0.117300
H    0.000000    0.757200   -0.469200
H    0.000000   -0.757200   -0.469200
*end
